<title>USA: IFC adds four countries to investable index.</title>
<headline>IFC adds four countries to investable index.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corp on Monday said that it had added the equities of Russia, Morocco, Egypt and Slovakia to its so-called Investable Index of emerging markets.</p>
<p>The World Bank affiliate, which helps the promote private sector development, said that brings the total to 30 countries that is in the so-called Investable List.</p>
<p>The IFC also publishes a separate Global List of emerging markets.</p>
</text>
